# The build context for tools/runner/Dockerfile is the REPOSITORY ROOT, because
# the Dockerfile COPYs tools/runner/runner.env. Without this file that context is
# the whole working tree — including a ~7 GB CD rip and node_modules.
#
# BuildKit only transfers what a COPY actually asks for, so the build is fast
# either way. This exists for the case that stops being true: someone adds a
# `COPY . .` and silently bakes the rip into a layer that could be pushed to a
# registry. Excluding it here makes that impossible rather than unlikely.

gamefiles
node_modules
dist
out
dfet
docs/.vitepress/cache
docs/.vitepress/dist
.git

# never let a credential into a build context
tools/runner/*.secret
*.pem
*.key

# large local artefacts that no image needs
public/nightdive.mov
public/collection
